  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 134 PM MDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nTuesday appears to be the next uptick in storm coverage, especially \nnortheast NM where a remnant convective outflow boundary may become \ndraped along the Sangre de Cristo Mts. Confidence is only moderate \nsince the only noteworthy change is the surface boundary. H5 temps \nremain close to -3C with the 597dm high center near northern NM. \nPWATs will remain >1\" so locally heavy rainfall is likely wherever \ncells do form. It will stay hot as well with more Heat Advisories \nlikely for a few zones Tuesday.\n\nFor Wednesday thru Saturday, the upper level high center continues \ndrifting west across northern NM with a slight decrease in forecast \nPWATs noted at KABQ. Otherwise, it will remain hot with an extended\nperiod of Heat Advisories for at least a few zones each day. Storm\ncoverage will vary from day to day with slight changes in steering\nflow across the region.",
